%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1963640d94415114d8eb3f359d5b928b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Scene Two (Tavern)_DialogueData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueSO
  locationDialogue: Tavern
  dialogueLines:
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: O THE LAST DEMON LORD THIS COUNTRY WILL EVER SEE! (slams mug down,
      ale sloshing everywhere) And to the guy who put an arrow through its eye socket
      from four hundred meters, HALF-DRUNK, might I add-
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: I was not half-drunk.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: You smelled half-drunk.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: That was the demon. Demons smell like a bar fight.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (dryly, not looking up) Four hundred and twelve years old, and
      I have never once heard either of you be right about anything on the first
      try.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: She wounds me. Right here. (thumps chest) In the honor.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: Your honor will survive. It's survived worse than me.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (small, tired smile, staring at his cup) ...It's over, huh.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: (quieter, catching the shift) Yeah. It is.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: You say that like it's a bad thing.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: "No. No, I just\u2014 (exhales) I don't know what a Tuesday looks
      like anymore. I've had a bow in my hand since I was eleven. I don't know what
      my hands are for if they're not doing that."
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: Drinking, apparently. You're doing great at that part.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (raises an eyebrow, finally looks at him properly) You "bought
      something." That sentence has never once ended well when you've said it.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: A floating island. Small one. Way out past the northern currents.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: (genuinely stunned, mug frozen halfway to his mouth) You bought
      a WHAT-
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: I'm gonna build a garden.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: (Beat of silence.)
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: A. Garden.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: A garden.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: The man who once shot a wyvern out of the sky mid-barrel-roll wants
      to grow... turnips.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: Tomatoes, probably. Turnips are a stretch goal.
  - characterName: ' Priestess'
    dialogueLine: (quiet, and this time genuinely warm) ...Good.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: '"Good"?? He''s throwing his LIFE-'
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: 'He''s keeping his life, you overgrown battering ram. That''s the
      part none of you ever learn until it''s already run out. '
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (to Archer, gentler) Go grow your tomatoes. Someone in this story
      deserves to see how it ends without a sword in their hand.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (raises his cup slightly) ...To after.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: (after a beat, grudgingly raising his too, grinning) To after.
      Gods help those tomatoes.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: (catching his breath from laughing) So what, you're just gonna
      go grow tomatoes and forget the last ten years happened?
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (shrugs, digs in his coat pocket, sets something small on the table,
      doesn't make a show of it) Not forget. Just... plant something that isn't a
      corpse count for once.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (glances at the object, tilts her head slightly) ...Where did you
      get that?
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: Found it. Somewhere around the Tree, on the way back. Half-buried,
      glowing a little. Figured a seed that survives a hundred years under a demon's
      throne's earned a nicer place to grow than a battlefield.
  - characterName: Blade Master
    dialogueLine: (squinting at it) ...Huh. Doesn't look like anything special.
  - characterName: Priestess
    dialogueLine: (quiet, not quite convinced, but lets it go, for now) No. It doesn't.
  - characterName: Archer
    dialogueLine: (pockets it again, lighter tone) Yeah, well. Neither did I, and
      look how that turned out.
